    "q-80667": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80667",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}10x+6y \\\\ 25x+15y\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $\\,u=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $\\,k\\,$ such that $\\,u\\in \\text{Ker}(T).$",
      "worked_solution": "A vector $u$ belongs to the kernel of a linear transformation $T$ if $T(u)=0.$ \n\nSo, we need to solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(u) & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10\\cdot k+6\\cdot 5 \\\\ 25\\cdot k+15\\cdot 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10k+30 \\\\ 25k+75\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}10k+30=0 \\\\ 25k+75=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to both of these equations is $k=-3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
