    "q-140066": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140066",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Given the linear transformation\n $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y-x-4z \\\\ 2x+7z-6y \\\\ 16z+4x-12y\\end{aligned}],$ find $\\text{nullity}(T).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write down the standard matrix of $T:$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 16\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(T)).$\n\nIn order to find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(T)),$ we reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 16\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 16\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has $1$ non-pivot columns (the 2nd one).  Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(T))=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
